# PHASE 02 — EDUCATION CONTROLLER INTEGRATION

## 2.1 Integration Package

Use the supplied Foundry Education Controller package.

Expected files:

- `foundry-education-controller.mjs`
- `foundry-controller-preview.html`
- `FOUNDRY_CONTROLLER_README.md`

Inspect the actual exported module API before integration.

Use `mountEducationController()` to initialize the supplied controller if confirmed by the module.

Do not recreate the Education Controller using new React components or generate a replacement interface.

## 2.2 Mounting Architecture

Mount the Education Controller in a dedicated viewport-level overlay layer above the Foundry canvas.

Maintain separate layers:

```text
Foundry Root
├── Canvas Layer
│   ├── Grid
│   ├── Drawing Objects
│   ├── Frames
│   ├── Connections
│   └── Interactive HTML Objects
│
├── Canvas Tools Layer
│
├── Floating Workspace Layer
│   ├── Education Controller
│   ├── External Application Panels
│   └── Future Controllers
│
├── Dialog Layer
└── Notification Layer
```

The floating workspace layer must remain independent of canvas transformations.

Canvas panning, zooming, and perspective changes must not move or scale the Education Controller.

## 2.3 Default Controller Placement

Position the Education Controller in the upper-left region of the Foundry workspace.

The controller should:

- Open at its compact default dimensions.
- Fit within the available viewport.
- Preserve its original proportions where practical.
- Remain draggable.
- Remain independently resizable.
- Remember its saved position and dimensions.

Do not add an external title bar, border, window frame, or duplicate control system.

## 2.4 Preserve Controller Functionality

Preserve the supplied controller's existing features:

- White minimize and restore dot.
- Blue expand and restore dot.
- Navigation-only minimized mode.
- Draggable positioning.
- External L-shaped resize handle.
- Independent width and height resizing.
- Middle divider resizing.
- Expandable navigation menu.
- Course selection menu.
- Profile panel.
- Session timer and projects.
- AI Chat.
- Knowledge Base.
- App Library.
- Account Settings.
- AI Management Settings.

Preserve the existing educational applications:

- Choice Board Studio.
- Essay to Slides.
- Countdown.
- Finals Study Guide.
- Digital Flashcards Studio.
- Student Command Center.
- Universal Design Lesson Planner.

Do not mark applications or external integrations as operational if they are only prototypes.

## 2.5 External Companion Panels

All companion application panels must open outside the main Education Controller.

Requirements:

- Default 24px separation.
- Independent dimensions.
- Independent resize controls.
- No parent controller scrollbars.
- No automatic enlargement of the main controller.
- No clipping inside the controller iframe.
- No duplicate application instances.
- Preserve application state when hidden.
- Maintain logical relationships with their parent controller.

The profile and session timer panel should also open externally.

When available space is limited, calculate an alternate visible position rather than creating unwanted parent scrolling.

## 2.6 Central AI Entry Point

The existing Education AI Chat must become Foundry's primary AI interface.

Route the native Foundry AI button to the supplied controller's `openAI()` method, if available.

If the controller is minimized:

1. Restore the controller.
2. Open AI Chat.
3. Bring the controller into focus.

Do not create a second AI chat interface.

Do not connect new AI providers during Stage 1.

